cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "tabletop: a complete factor grid in colour, depth and words"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Anoop
    family-names: Kaithalikunnel Chandran
    email: anoopkcn@gmail.com
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/anoopkcn/tabletop"
keywords:
  - disentanglement
  - representation learning
  - multimodal
  - RGB-D
  - synthetic dataset
abstract: >-
  One object on a table, seen by a colour camera and a depth camera from the
  same viewpoint and described in words. Every state of a complete seven-factor
  grid (shape, hue, size, rotation, position, light, table; 294,912 states) is
  rendered once by a self-contained ray caster, so the dataset is reproducible
  from its source alone. Two factors are periodic with a known period, two are
  straight lines in the world, and three (hue, light, table colour) are absent
  from the depth image by construction, which puts a known ceiling on what a
  depth encoder can resolve. The nuisance is explicit and adjustable: camera
  pitch and yaw jitter drawn independently per camera, and Gaussian pixel noise
  on RGB. A nuisance-free twin of the grid is provided as a control.
